#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192655 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192586 :question/id #uuid "eb7f1f32-1a5c-526e-878b-8046c4feb8c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-13997" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n${3x + 4y = 2; x - 2y = 4$\n\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $y$ from this system by filling in the missing information below.\n\n$\\qquad$ *To eliminate $y$, multiply the $\\,\\textbf{__________}\\,$equation by $\\,\\textbf{______}\\,$,\nand add the equations.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $y$ in the first equation is $4$, while in the second equation it is $-2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by ${\\color{blue}2}$, then the coefficient of $y$ will turn into $-4$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $4$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n{(3x + 4y = 2; (x - 2y = 4)\\cdot (2)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x + 4y &= 2 \\\\\n2x - 4y &= 8 \\\\\n(3x + 2x) &= (2 + 8) \\\\\n5x &= 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $y$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{second}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}2}$, and add the equations*."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e7bfcbe-4913-53e0-98c7-171965adfe62" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508377 :question-generator/id #uuid "835d8836-7a8d-5bd9-ad81-8fb2ebfafdee" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186192655.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "805f8ad6-7fae-5b23-9e8d-6ae094055dbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191254} {:answer/id #uuid "90021633-7a04-57cc-a6b7-c9aa58120746" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191255}