nteger multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $y$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $y$ in the first equation is $-1$, while in the second equation it is $-2$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-2}$, then the coefficient of $y$ will turn into $2$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-2$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(-3x - y = 5)\\cdot (-2); -8x - 2y = 3\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x + 2y &= -10 \\\\\n-8x - 2y &= 3 \\\\\n(6x - 8x) &= (-10 + 3) \\\\\n-2x &= -7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $y$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-2}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508327 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1492c2d9-3b96-5d99-af2f-6e353ea4288a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508256} {:answer/id #uuid "3c58fb78-1c5a-5c15-a174-22de3ccedad7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508277} {:answer/id #uuid "41e49d7e-68bc-5ebc-a9ef-96bd0d52383e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508281} {:answer/id #uuid "fb4f2e04-8657-5d5c-84fc-fa0044c746d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41e49d7e-68bc-5ebc-a9ef-96bd0d52383e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508281} :answer-field/id #uuid "6286a964-ba5c-565d-8d4e-a9e48c8480d3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508306} {:answer-field/choi