\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $4$, while in the second equation it is $-24$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}6}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $24$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-24$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(-8a + 4b = 5)\\cdot (6); -2a - 24b = 5\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-48a + 24b &= 30 \\\\\n-2a - 24b &= 5 \\\\\n(-48a - 2a) &= (30 + 5) \\\\\n-50a &= 35\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}6}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508349 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3329bb61-ee30-5582-b95e-93e49d25acbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508272} {:answer/id #uuid "5745dbcd-d2ec-538d-a5c0-6e40a55ff9c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5745dbcd-d2ec-538d-a5c0-6e40a55ff9c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508297} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b6e85c3-b039-528d-a630-269f4ab66bb7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508309} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7589e36d-b3bd-5962-bc29-ef4192f475f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508313} {:answer/id #uuid "c7eecde5-9335-5d7e-894a-906a63b21f24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508346} {:answer/id #uuid "c93a3f98-da46-5359-80b0-24e43b80b96b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508347} {:answer/id #uuid "d016ec66-1262-59a6-a15b-893c32493375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7589e36d-b3bd-5962-bc29-ef4192f475f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508313} :answer-field/id #uuid "873c2de2-15f7-503c-a9ac-a78b7c9793bb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508320}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cbd0b334-3f69-5bfe-96e0-237eb18aaf58" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$\\{a - b = -6; -7a - 3b = 9$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $-1$, while in the second equation it is $-3$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-3}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $3$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-3$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(a - b = -6)\\cdot (-3); -7a - 3b = 9\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3a + 3b &= 18 \\\\\n-7a - 3b &= 9 \\\\\n(-3a - 7a) &= (18 + 9) \\\\\n-10a &= 27\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-3}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508354 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39a6814c-18ed-51c5-ac72-0b9e8d2d7b22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508276} {:answer/id #uuid "b370d6a5-ae0f-513a-be14-2ead2c5dd0ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b370d6a5-ae0f-513a-be14-2ead2c5dd0ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508338} :answer-field/id #uuid "15446ed6-06ee-5e8f-b9db-fb23758c2828" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508257} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e3b6170-053d-5e20-bf03-eb7b7f0b9b9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508271} {:answer/id #uuid "34c59b71-7028-5a50-90c2-416e17328ce0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508274} {:answer/id #uuid "898c0b7e-ab07-55a0-9d3e-8d2228d97878" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508323} {:answer/id #uuid "8e9898c4-dfc7-5d09-b10e-60992932dae0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e3b6170-053d-5e20-bf03-eb7b7f0b9b9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508271} :answer-field/id #uuid "5245f9d9-ac94-562c-8092-471960c6d9fc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508292}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d1ff7503-ea2c-53d8-b2dc-feb812e688fc" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{6x - y = 8; -6x + 2y = 6$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $y$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $y$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $y$ in the first equation is $-1$, while in the second equation it is $2$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}2}$, then the coefficient of $y$ will turn into $-2$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $2$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(6x - y = 8)\\cdot (2); -6x + 2y = 6\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n12x - 2y &= 16 \\\\\n-6x + 2y &= 6 \\\\\n(12x - 6x) &= (16 + 6) \\\\\n6x &= 22\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $y$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}2}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508360 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "225d1f98-8b27-555d-afa6-e6d941ada34c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508264} {:answer/id #uuid "dc1678d3-65a7-531d-aee9-ccee73215a8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508356} {:answer/id #uuid "dfcb8d2b-1f63-5290-bbaf-e02572a87ce1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508357} {:answer/id #uuid "e7a4499a-ae96-5717-b6b6-6daef56eb4cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "225d1f98-8b27-555d-afa6-e6d941ada34c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508264} :answer-field/id #uuid "07170df4-3002-5d99-8a83-98dd811ef120" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508245} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21b689ce-4bcb-548c-8656-608257bc0e48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508262} {:answer/id #uuid "57d446a3-0af8-50b0-b18a-e196585ca47d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21b689ce-4bcb-548c-8656-608257bc0e48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508262} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e9670cb-e167-5a08-925c-656947a40567" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508288}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e241fcce-6c28-5eb1-91b2-aee856170291" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$\\{10a + b = -1; 9a + 5b = -5$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $1$, while in the second equation it is $5$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-5}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $-5$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $5$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(10a + b = -1)\\cdot (-5); 9a + 5b = -5\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-50a - 5b &= 5 \\\\\n9a + 5b &= -5 \\\\\n(-50a + 9a) &= (5 - 5) \\\\\n-41a &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-5}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508365 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09e8579d-b157-52e9-b7ed-5985f9e85259" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508248} {:answer/id #uuid "134fb8c9-6ede-56c5-bc4e-c5e8ccaabe65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508255} {:answer/id #uuid "d09d4f07-de21-5249-aa7b-ff1686f1e146" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508353} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e111be-bf81-5801-bc93-3b2bad662b63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09e8579d-b157-52e9-b7ed-5985f9e85259" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508248} :answer-field/id #uuid "074e8cbb-4ae9-5dfc-ad31-766133a53fe3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508246} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e0e218a-1bf4-5098-b918-d285259aca08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508324} {:answer/id #uuid "d9f60b70-b8c2-5448-9297-4b52ef616717" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e0e218a-1bf4-5098-b918-d285259aca08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508324} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d1c3c66-66ba-5111-9e0a-80d446b48de7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508301}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e58c3e5b-b391-5afd-9ee6-da3df80ea5cd" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$\\{a - 3b = -6; -7a - 6b = 9$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $-3$, while in the second equation it is $-6$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-2}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $6$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-6$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(a - 3b = -6)\\cdot (-2); -7a - 6b = 9\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2a + 6b &= 12 \\\\\n-7a - 6b &= 9 \\\\\n(-2a - 7a) &= (12 + 9) \\\\\n-9a &= 21\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-2}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508370 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2830d30e-f96c-5c09-a79c-8a94e978b292" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508266} {:answer/id #uuid "5518e6b8-b214-5f7b-a5de-7f4b43b00897" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508295} {:answer/id #uuid "82fdb308-ba8c-5c51-a928-c4e4aa5c60e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508318} {:answer/id #uuid "a7870df0-e865-550b-8098-64365d920e80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7870df0-e865-550b-8098-64365d920e80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508335} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cba64b5-9bf1-503e-b1b2-39e507432e1a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508278} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5000535-be94-5ca1-b227-8c4b08b24908" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508344} {:answer/id #uuid "fa2063e0-c497-5fb3-8b39-0ed66ba354d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa2063e0-c497-5fb3-8b39-0ed66ba354d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508374} :answer-field/id #uuid "4689c9a4-33eb-5422-8dc1-46ed14684c4f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508283}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f40ec0f3-3ce5-52b3-a3e7-9ca324b7f03c" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{5a - 4b = 6; 8a - 12b = -6$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $-4$, while in the second equation it is $-12$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-3}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $12$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-12$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(5a - 4b = 6)\\cdot (-3); 8a - 12b = -6\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-15a + 12b &= -18 \\\\\n8a - 12b &= -6 \\\\\n(-15a + 8a) &= (-18 - 6) \\\\\n-7a &= -24\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-3}$, and add the equations*."}] :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the Second Variable"}]}
